    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Visitors can paddle non‑motorized boats, but must wash them at the on‑site boat washing station before entering the lakes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mountainlakesnh.com/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The community covers about 17 miles of roads, 75 acres of open water across two lakes, and an additional 25 acres of wetlands.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mountainlakesnh.com/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Mountain Lakes preserves 570 acres of common “green belt” that hosts numerous nature trails and wildlife habitats.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mountainlakesnh.com/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The recreation area includes a softball field, volleyball court, playground, horseshoe pits, picnic tables with umbrellas, and barbecue grills.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.mountainlakesnh.com/about"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Motorized boats and other craft are expressly forbidden from the lakes and beaches, keeping the waters calm and safe for families.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
